  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 1980s Washington, a colonel named Hohman is said to have helped sell Ronald Reagan on SDI, the Strategic Defense Initiative, his planned shield against missiles from space, by pointing to an alien threat the people involved knew was false. A guest named Steven Greer says Hohman told him this himself: \"We knew that was false, but it got billions of dollars for SDI.\" If true, it would mean the alien idea was used on purpose to win money for weapons."
}
